.TH DRAGONGL-CLIENT 1 "2026-11-08" "DragonGL 2026.11.08.11" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
dragongl-client \- Dragon GL client launcher script
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dragongl-client
[\fIserver_host\fR [\fIport\fR]]
.br
.B dragongl-client
.BR \-h " | " \-\-help
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B dragongl-client
starts
.BR dragongl_client (1):
the one installed next to the script (RPM:
.IR /usr/bin ),
or
.I build/dragongl_client
in a development tree. The arguments are passed on unchanged; the working
directory does not matter (the client finds its shaders next to the
executable or in
.IR /usr/share/dragongl/shaders ).
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.I server_host
(optional) Host name, IPv4 or IPv6 address of the server; skips the
interactive prompt (handy over SSH).
.TP
.I port
(optional) Server TCP port (default 8080).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show a short help message and exit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
See
.BR dragongl_client (1):
.BR DRAGONGL_WINDOW ,
.BR DRAGONGL_GPU ,
.BR DRAGONGL_VSYNC ,
.BR DRAGONGL_SHADER_DIR ,
.BR VK_INSTANCE_LAYERS .
.SH EXAMPLES
Start the client and answer the prompts:
.PP
.RS
.B dragongl-client
.RE
.PP
Connect directly to a remote server:
.PP
.RS
.B dragongl-client 192.168.1.10 9000
.br
.B dragongl-client 2001:db8::10
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR dragongl_client (1),
.BR dragongl-server (1)
